  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A work board lists routine tasks, their expected effort, and the volunteers who can take them.\", \"decision\": \"How should unclaimed routine work be allocated?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteers claim tasks from the work board, then the coordinator asks for help with unclaimed work. Self-selection handles most allocation before gaps receive attention.\nThe coordinator proposes task assignments on the work board, then volunteers exchange unsuitable tasks. A complete initial allocation can be corrected by the people doing the work.\nVolunteers rank tasks on the work board, then the coordinator assigns work using those preferences and expected effort. Preferences inform a more balanced distribution of work."
    }
  ],
